From: Om Swami <reach.oms2004@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:44:13 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(client): sign inputs with keys held by an external
 signer

A module whose spend keys live elsewhere, such as on a hardware signer with
a trusted display, marks inputs with `ClientInputBundle::with_remote_keys`.
The client then builds the transaction unsigned, computes the operation
meta, and asks the `TransactionSigner` set with
`ClientBuilder::with_transaction_signer` for one signature per remote key,
checking each before it submits.

`TransactionBuilder::build` keeps signing local keys as before;
`build_unsigned` and `UnsignedTransaction::sign` split it for remote keys.
